<lane ...input id="lavra" name="Lavra"
  by="Roberto Mello · Claude Code, OpenCode, Gemini CLI, Cortex Code" source=lavra>
  <@summary>
    Extends Compound Engineering. The plan is an epic with child issues ("beads") in the Beads tracker, not a file. A hook asks a subagent to log what it learned before it stops, but does not check that it did.
  </@summary>
  <@order label="Order, per the author" lead="recommended in docs; the human types each command">
    "Most of the time, you type three commands": <command-ref of=lavra name="lavra-design" path="plugins/lavra/commands/lavra-design.md"/>, <command-ref of=lavra name="lavra-work" path="plugins/lavra/commands/lavra-work.md"/>, <command-ref of=lavra name="lavra-ship" path="plugins/lavra/commands/lavra-ship.md"/>, with <command-ref of=lavra name="lavra-qa" path="plugins/lavra/commands/lavra-qa.md"/> optional for web apps (README.md). Inside <command-ref of=lavra name="lavra-design" path="plugins/lavra/commands/lavra-design.md"/> the phases chain: "Brainstorm → Plan → Research → Revise → CEO Review → Eng Review → Lock". Review and the fix loop run inside <command-ref of=lavra name="lavra-work" path="plugins/lavra/commands/lavra-work.md"/>. <command-ref of=lavra name="lavra-quick"/> is a shortcut for small tasks.
  </@order>
  <@owner from="brainstorm" to="review-lock" name="lavra-design" note="command; chains six phases"/>
  <@owner from="execute-beads" to="review-goal-verify" name="lavra-work"
    note="command; routes to single, sequential or parallel"/>
  <@owner from="browser-qa" to="browser-qa" name="lavra-qa" note="command; optional"/>
  <@owner from="ship" to="ship" name="lavra-ship" note="command"/>
  <@owner from="knowledge-capture" to="knowledge-capture" name="hooks.json"
    note="hook configuration: four harness events, no command"/>
  <@cover col="req" level="explicit">Requirements and Non-Requirements on the epic</@cover>
  <@cover col="base" level="implicit">
    research agents run inside Plan; deeper research off by default
  </@cover>
  <@cover col="design" level="implicit">Locked Decisions; no design document</@cover>
  <@cover col="tasks" level="explicit">child beads, DAG validated</@cover>
  <@cover col="verify" level="implicit">per bead; the epic requirements are not rechecked</@cover>
  <@cover col="learn" level="explicit">memory file; a hook asks, nothing checks</@cover>
  <@take>
    Every decision typed Locked, Discretion or Deferred; reviewers get the Locked list so they do not flag planned gaps.
  </@take>
  <@take>
    <agent-ref of=lavra name="goal-verifier" path="plugins/lavra/agents/review/goal-verifier.md"/> levels: exists, substantive, wired. Catches stubs and unconnected code.
  </@take>
  <@take>
    Parallel waves by file ownership: beads that touch the same file get a dependency; subagents may not commit.
  </@take>
  <@gap>
    Gates are checklists the agent fills in about itself; the stop hook asks for a learning and never checks for one.
  </@gap>
  <@gap>Nothing rechecks the epic requirements after the beads pass.</@gap>
  <@gap>Ship ends at the PR.</@gap>
  <@gap>
    Two hook scripts call code that is not there: <script-ref of=lavra name="extract-bead-context.sh" path="plugins/lavra/hooks/extract-bead-context.sh"/> looks for <script-ref of=lavra name="sanitize-content.sh" path="plugins/lavra/hooks/sanitize-content.sh"/> one directory too high and exits with an error; check-memory.sh calls a function that only the installer defines.
  </@gap>

